<title>UK: FORECAST - Reuters foreign exchange poll - June.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Reuters foreign exchange poll - June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The dollar is expected to fall steadily against mark and yen over the next 12 months, according to a consensus of 31 banks and financial institutions from around the globe polled by Reuters on June 3 and 4.</p>
<p>The averages of the forecasts were as follows,</p>
<p>			   1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	 12-MTH</p>
<p>    STERLING/DOLLAR  1.6298     1.6271     1.6216	1.6179</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/MARK	1.7197     1.6982     1.6814	1.6423</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/YEN	 116.26     115.38     113.57	110.10</p>
<p>Using the dollar forecasts above, the cross rates calculate at:--</p>
<p>			    1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	12-MTH</p>
<p>    STERLING/MARK     2.8028     2.7633     2.7265     2.6572</p>
<p>    MARK/YEN	    67.61	67.94	67.55	67.04</p>
<p>At 1000 GMT, the dollar was trading at 1.7313/18 marks and 116.24/29 yen. Sterling/dollar was quoted at $1.6342/52, sterling/mark at 2.8305/12 and mark/yen at 67.14/16.</p>
<p>The minimum and maximum forecasts were as follows --</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/MARK	1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	 12-MTH</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    1.6650     1.6300     1.5500	1.5000</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    1.7550     1.7800     1.8000	1.8000</p>
<p>DOLLAR/YEN</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    112.00     108.00     108.00	102.00</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    120.00     122.00     120.00	120.00</p>
<p>STERLING/DOLLAR</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    1.5850     1.5800     1.5500	1.4500</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    1.6500     1.6950     1.7250	1.8050</p>
<p>The dollar is expected to weaken during the next month to trade at 1.7197 marks before continuing the trend to trade at 1.6814 by the end of 1997, this trend is then expected remain with the dollar/mark trading at 1.6423 in a year from now.</p>
<p>The highest the dollar is expected to climb is to 1.8000 marks during this period, the lowest it is predicted to fall is to 1.5000 marks.</p>
<p>Against the yen, the dollar is expected to remain close to current levels during the next month before slipping to 115.38 in three months time. It is then expected to continue on a slippery slope to trade at 113.57 in six months before falling further to trade at 110.10 in a year from now.</p>
<p>The lowest dollar/yen is expected to trade during the next twelve months is 102.00. The highest it is expected to trade at is 122.00, which could be reached during the next three months according to one forecaster.</p>
<p>The poll showed sterling mapping a steady decline against the dollar. Forecasters expect the pound to struggle to trade at 1.6298 in one month, continuing its decline to 1.6271 in three months from now. Cable is then expected to weaken even further to trade at $1.6179 in a year from now.</p>
<p>The lowest level sterling is expected to fall to during the next twelve months is $1.4500, the highest it is expected to climb to is $1.8050.</p>
<p>The rankings of the 31 forecasters polled by the accuracy of their one-month predictions will be published in the first week of July, just before the results of the next poll.</p>
